<Base title="When words feel difficult" description="A few gentle starting points for a page that feels hard to begin."><article class="prose"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / When words feel difficult</nav><p class="eyebrow">Bloom Library · Reflection</p><h1>When words feel difficult</h1><p class="smallnote">New editorial draft · I Will Bloom · 17 November 2026</p><p>A blank page can feel like an invitation. On another day, it can feel like another thing asking something of you.</p><p>You do not need to make a record of everything. You might begin with a colour, the weather outside, or one word that feels close enough.</p><h2>Try a smaller beginning</h2><ul><li>Today feels…</li><li>Something I wish I could say is…</li><li>For the next hour, I would like…</li></ul><p>You can stop there. A sentence does not need to become a story. A page does not need to be finished to have held something for you.</p><p><a href="/bloom-library/">← Back to the Bloom Library</a></p></article></Base>